Subject: [PATCH] Read EGL default framebuffer without an invalid object lookup

Name zero selects the EGL read surface. The user-framebuffer lookup queues
INVALID_OPERATION for zero, contaminating a successful native surface read.
Use that lookup only for nonzero names, retaining its validation for FBOs.

Apply after 0012.

diff --git a/src/emu/dispatch/src/libraries/gles2/gles2.cpp b/src/emu/dispatch/src/libraries/gles2/gles2.cpp
--- a/src/emu/dispatch/src/libraries/gles2/gles2.cpp
+++ b/src/emu/dispatch/src/libraries/gles2/gles2.cpp
@@ -3064,7 +3064,11 @@
 
         dispatcher *dp = sys->get_dispatcher();
         dispatch::egl_controller &controller = dp->get_egl_controller();
-        gles_framebuffer_object *fb_obj = get_binded_framebuffer_object_gles(ctx, controller);
+        // Name zero is the valid EGL read surface, not a user framebuffer.
+        // The object lookup reports INVALID_OPERATION for zero, even though
+        // the default-surface read below succeeds.
+        gles_framebuffer_object *fb_obj = ctx->binded_framebuffer_
+            ? get_binded_framebuffer_object_gles(ctx, controller) : nullptr;
 
         // Framebuffer handle on driver side still 0 = not drawn anything yet. Don't waste time
         // Maybe we should still read though. No one knows
